  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Color noise ist the result of a collaboration between the artist Kiki Smith and the printmaking department of the Savannah College of Art and Design in Atlanta, GA. It was printed by master printer Robert T. Brown with the assistance of students Laura Cleary, Sara Hemingway, Nate Kamp, and Ashley L. Schick. It is digitally printed on Awagami Inbe thick white digital inkjet paper (125g) and lithographically printed on Japanese M20 Gamp White. It is published by the Southeastern Center for Printmaking in an edition of 13, with 1 B.A.T., 4 artists' proofs, 5 printers proofs, and 1 archival impression in the year 2012"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">One continuous sheet folded accordion-style, comprising 10 panels. The top sections of five of the panels feature each a slightly altered lithographed portrait of the artist, the bottem parts consist of pastel colored tissue paper which appears to be floating below the portraits.</subfield>
  </datafield>
